{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7f3c1a2-9d4e-4f18-8c62-1a5e7d3b9f04",
    "name": "Sentinel API",
    "description": "Sentinel Backend — Express + Drizzle.\n\nGrows one folder per module. Sprint 1 ships `Auth` and `Users`; `Vendors` and `Transactions` land next, and the Sprint 2 AI service (`/analyze`, `/chat`) lives in a separate repo and collection.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import `sentinel_local.postman_environment.json` and select it.\n2. Seed a Finance Lead: `npm run db:seed -- lead@company.com \"Nama\"`.\n3. Put that email and password into the `seedEmail` / `seedPassword` variables.\n4. Run **Auth → Login (password)**. It captures `accessToken` and `refreshToken` automatically — every other request reuses them, so no copy-pasting.\n\n## Order that works end to end\nLogin → Users: Create member (captures `memberId` + `tempPassword`) → Users: List → Users: Deactivate member.\n\n`Guards` holds the negative cases. They are meant to fail with a specific status, and their tests assert exactly that — a green run there means the API is refusing what it should.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5000/api/v1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "healthUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5000/health",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{healthUrl}}",
          "host": [
            "{{healthUrl}}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
